WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:00.973
- All right.

00:00:00.973 --> 00:00:02.470
(clap)
Hey guys, it's me, Jasmine.

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:04.740
We are here at Sushi Ginza Onodera,

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:06.370
a two Michelin star restaurant.

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:07.720
We're gonna speak with Chef Yohei

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:10.660
and he's gonna show us a
little bit about aging fish,

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.750
a super, super traditional process

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.980
that dates back to 200 years ago.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:15.881
Let's go check it out.

00:00:15.881 --> 00:00:17.010
(drum banging)

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.235
Like a party in my mouth.

00:00:18.235 --> 00:00:19.678
- Oh, enjoy party (speaks
in foreign language)

00:00:19.678 --> 00:00:21.560
(laughter)

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.390
- Americans are obsessed with fresh sushi.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.480
We want the fish to be caught, prepared,

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.870
and placed on our plate
all on the same day.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.020
But in order for that
delectable piece of toro

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:34.960
to go from boat to tongue,
it has to travel a long way.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.700
So how do you preserve that
fresh taste that we all crave?

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.052
Well by freezing it.

00:00:39.052 --> 00:00:42.885
(speaks in foreign language)

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:43.340
- There are many ways to age fish

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:45.870
but the four main
techniques in Edomae sushi

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:49.060
are one, konbujime,
salted seaweed marinade,

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:51.710
two, shoyu-zuke, a soy sauce marinade,

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:54.270
three, sujime, a pickling
vinegar marinade,

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:57.728
and four, nimono, cooking the fish.

00:01:57.728 --> 00:02:00.750
(drum beating)

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:04.302
First, seaweed is rehydrated
using sake until soft.

00:02:04.302 --> 00:02:07.190
(upbeat music)

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:09.680
Then the filet is salted
and wrapped in the seaweed

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:13.163
like a blanket, then left
to age for four days.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:16.570
Kochi is a white fish

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:18.873
with similar texture to the puffer fish.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:24.986
(speaks in foreign language)

00:02:24.986 --> 00:02:25.819
- Mmmm.

00:02:27.257 --> 00:02:28.858
(speaks in foreign language)

00:02:28.858 --> 00:02:29.691
- That was so good.

00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:30.720
There's like a bounce to it,

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.978
like Christmas every 30 seconds.

00:02:32.978 --> 00:02:35.940
(drum beating)

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:37.460
The salmon is quickly poached

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:40.810
in a bath of hot water
and cooled in an ice bath

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:42.970
to prevent cooking all the way through.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:44.810
Then the filet is placed in a marinade

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.840
of homemade soy sauce, mirin, and dashi,

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:49.651
then aged for one night.

00:02:49.651 --> 00:02:52.068
(calm music)

00:03:03.334 --> 00:03:04.167
Mmm.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:06.400
Melts in my mouth.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:09.740
And I know it's aged, but
it just tastes so, so fresh.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:10.598
- Thank you much.

00:03:10.598 --> 00:03:13.570
(drum beating)

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:14.920
- After the fish is fileted,

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.140
it's placed in a strong salt water bath

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:20.530
for 10 minutes to remove
that strong, fishy smell.

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:22.330
The skin is torched very slightly

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:25.143
and placed in a bowl of
vinegar for 30 minutes.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:28.370
After, the skin is scored and topped with

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:30.633
original Japanese tiger shrimp powder.

00:03:32.817 --> 00:03:36.567
(speaks in foreign language)

00:03:39.057 --> 00:03:39.890
Mmm.

00:03:42.159 --> 00:03:43.460
I don't even know how to describe that.

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:44.645
Like a party in my mouth.

00:03:44.645 --> 00:03:47.597
- Yeah. Oh, enjoy party,
(speaks in foreign language)

00:03:47.597 --> 00:03:49.424
(laughter)

00:03:49.424 --> 00:03:52.730
(drum beating)

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:54.950
- The eel is fileted
then placed in hot water

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:57.470
to remove slime on the skin.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:01.450
Then it's cooked in a
soup base for 30 minutes.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:04.350
The soup base is kept and
used over again each time

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:06.833
enriching the flavor and
thickness of the broth.

00:04:11.406 --> 00:04:12.620
Mmm.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:13.520
So different.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:15.067
- Yes.
- But so delicious.

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:18.817
(speaks in foreign language)

00:04:44.714 --> 00:04:46.210
- Taking in the entire process,

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:49.600
it doesn't just start here,
it starts with the fishermen.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.880
And then you come and prep and do

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.500
all this beautiful stuff in between.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:55.230
And you say that the process ends with

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:56.710
the customer eating it.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:58.380
It's like a whole story.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:01.040
And you were saying how
it's like an open book.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:02.480
We see everything.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.130
So seeing the love and care that goes into

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:06.570
each single piece of fish,

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:07.620
I think that really makes it,

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:08.889
that sets it apart from everything.

00:05:08.889 --> 00:05:12.722
(speaks in foreign language)

